### =====================================================================
### RECHARGE NET — ARMAGEDDON TEST SUITE COMPLETA
### Copre: auth, boutique, tariffe, ricariche, fatture, dashboard, export
### Include: happy path, violazioni ownership, edge case, crash bait,
###          paradossi di stato, injection, sequenze illegali
### =====================================================================

@base = http://localhost:8080/api/v2


### =====================================================================
### SEZIONE 0 — LOGIN E TOKEN
### =====================================================================

### 0.1 Login SuperAdmin -> ATTESO: 200 + token
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"superadmin","password":"superadmin123"}

> {%
    client.global.set("tokenSuper", response.body.token);
%}

###

### 0.2 Login Admin A -> ATTESO: 200 + token
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"adminA","password":"adminA123"}

> {%
    client.global.set("tokenAdminA", response.body.token);
%}

###

### 0.3 Login Admin B -> ATTESO: 200 + token
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"adminB","password":"adminB123"}

> {%
    client.global.set("tokenAdminB", response.body.token);
%}

###

### 0.4 Login Dipendente A1 -> ATTESO: 200 + token
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"dipA1","password":"dipA1123"}

> {%
    client.global.set("tokenDipA1", response.body.token);
%}

###

### 0.5 Login Dipendente A2 -> ATTESO: 200 + token
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"dipA2","password":"dipA2123"}

> {%
    client.global.set("tokenDipA2", response.body.token);
%}

###

### 0.6 Login Dipendente B1 -> ATTESO: 200 + token
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"dipB1","password":"dipB1123"}

> {%
    client.global.set("tokenDipB1", response.body.token);
%}

###

### 0.7 [CRASH BAIT] Login con body completamente vuoto -> ATTESO: 400 (non 500)
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{}

###

### 0.8 [CRASH BAIT] Login con password sbagliata -> ATTESO: 401
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"adminA","password":"SBAGLIATA"}

###

### 0.9 [SECURITY] Login senza Content-Type -> ATTESO: 400 o 415
POST {{base}}/auth/login

{"username":"adminA","password":"adminA123"}

###

### 0.10 [SECURITY] Token Bearer assente su endpoint protetto -> ATTESO: 401
GET {{base}}/boutique

###

### 0.11 [SECURITY] Token completamente inventato -> ATTESO: 401
GET {{base}}/boutique
Authorization: Bearer questo.token.efalso

###

### 0.12 [SECURITY] Token corretto ma senza prefisso Bearer -> ATTESO: 401
GET {{base}}/boutique
Authorization: {{tokenAdminA}}

###

### 0.13 [SECURITY] Token con Bearer ma valore vuoto -> ATTESO: 401
GET {{base}}/boutique
Authorization: Bearer

###


### =====================================================================
### SEZIONE 1 — SETUP: RECUPERO ID DINAMICI
### =====================================================================

### 1.1 Recupera boutique di Admin A (serve boutiqueA1_id e boutiqueA2_id)
GET {{base}}/boutique
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdminA}}

> {%
    client.global.set("boutiqueA1_id", response.body[0].id);
    client.global.set("boutiqueA2_id", response.body.length > 1 ? response.body[1].id : response.body[0].id);
%}

###

### 1.2 Recupera boutique di Admin B
GET {{base}}/boutique
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdminB}}

> {%
    client.global.set("boutiqueB1_id", response.body[0].id);
%}

###

### 1.3 SuperAdmin vede TUTTE le boutique del sistema -> ATTESO: 200 lista completa
GET {{base}}/boutique/tutte
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenSuper}}

###

### 1.4 [SECURITY] Admin A tenta di vedere tutte le boutique -> ATTESO: 403
GET {{base}}/boutique/tutte
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdminA}}

###

### 1.5 [SECURITY] Dipendente tenta di vedere tutte le boutique -> ATTESO: 403
GET {{base}}/boutique/tutte
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenDipA1}}

###


### =====================================================================
### SEZIONE 2 — UTENTI E ADMIN
### =====================================================================

### 2.1 SuperAdmin crea un nuovo Admin -> ATTESO: 200
POST {{base}}/utenti/admin
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenSuper}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"nome":"Admin Test","username":"adminTest","password":"password123"}

###

### 2.2 [SECURITY] Admin A tenta di creare un Admin -> ATTESO: 403
POST {{base}}/utenti/admin
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdminA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"nome":"Hacker Admin","username":"hacker","password":"hacker123"}

###

### 2.3 [SECURITY] Dipendente tenta di creare un Admin -> ATTESO: 403
POST {{base}}/utenti/admin
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenDipA1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"nome":"Dipendente Admin","username":"dipAdmin","password":"pass1234"}

###

### 2.4 [VALIDATION] Crea Admin con username troppo corto (< 3 char) -> ATTESO: 400
POST {{base}}/utenti/admin
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenSuper}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"nome":"X","username":"ab","password":"password123"}

###

### 2.5 [VALIDATION] Crea Admin con password troppo corta (< 8 char) -> ATTESO: 400
POST {{base}}/utenti/admin
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenSuper}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"nome":"Admin Corto","username":"admincorto","password":"abc"}

###

### 2.6 [VALIDATION] Crea Admin con body vuoto -> ATTESO: 400
POST {{base}}/utenti/admin
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenSuper}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

###

### 2.7 [CRASH BAIT] Username duplicato -> ATTESO: 400 o 500 se constraint non gestito
POST {{base}}/utenti/admin
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenSuper}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"nome":"Admin Duplicato","username":"adminA","password":"password123"}

###


### =====================================================================
### SEZIONE 3 — BOUTIQUE
### =====================================================================

### 3.1 [SECURITY] Dipendente tenta di creare boutique -> ATTESO: 403
POST {{base}}/boutique
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenDipA1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"nome":"Boutique Hacker","citta":"Napoli","usernameDipendente":"dipHack","passwordDipendente":"pass1234"}

###

### 3.2 [SECURITY] SuperAdmin tenta di creare boutique (solo ADMIN può) -> ATTESO: 403
POST {{base}}/boutique
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenSuper}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"nome":"Boutique Super","citta":"Roma","usernameDipendente":"dipSuper","passwordDipendente":"pass1234"}

###

### 3.3 [VALIDATION] Crea boutique senza nome -> ATTESO: 400
POST {{base}}/boutique
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdminA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"citta":"Tunisi","usernameDipendente":"dipNew","passwordDipendente":"pass1234"}

###

### 3.4 [VALIDATION] Crea boutique con body vuoto -> ATTESO: 400
POST {{base}}/boutique
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdminA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

###

### 3.5 [BUSINESS] Admin A crea boutique con nome duplicato (stesso admin) -> ATTESO: 400
POST {{base}}/boutique
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdminA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"nome":"Boutique A1","citta":"Tunisi","usernameDipendente":"dipDuplicato","passwordDipendente":"pass1234"}

###

### 3.6 [BUSINESS] Admin A crea boutique con username dipendente già esistente -> ATTESO: 400
POST {{base}}/boutique
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdminA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"nome":"Boutique Nuova","citta":"Tunisi","usernameDipendente":"dipA1","passwordDipendente":"pass1234"}

